WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:06.049
Going to the movies is fun, but actually making
those movies can be stressful, difficult,

00:00:06.049 --> 00:00:07.419
and even dangerous at times.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:12.040
In fact, there have been a number of stars
who nearly died during the filming of some

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:13.380
of your favorite movies.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.260
Here's a look at some iconic movie scenes
that nearly killed actors.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:18.740
Kevin Costner

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:23.280
You could safely say that there's never been
a better movie about post-apocalyptic boat

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.540
fights than Waterworld.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.820
But this supremely guilty pleasure didn't
just kill Kevin Costner's status as an A-list

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.260
star, it also nearly killed him period.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.520
While he was filming a scene that had him
tethered to the top of a sailboat's mast,

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:41.460
a sudden storm swept over the set and caught
Costner dangling from the rickety mast.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.300
Wind and waves smashed into him repeatedly,
but the squall made it too dangerous for the

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.460
crew to pull him down.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.450
According to People, Costner later told a
friend that he'd "almost died" during the

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:53.220
30-minute ordeal.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.300
Luckily, he had his own way of dealing with
the water.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:58.640
"Gills…

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.940
Mutation!"

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.720
"He's a muuuuuutaaaaaannnnnnttttt!!!!"

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.860
Jaimie Alexander

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.560
Superhero movies come with big action—and
even bigger safety precautions.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:17.400
And yet accidents can still happen, as actress
Jaimie Alexander, who plays Sif, unfortunately

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.000
found out on the set of Thor: The Dark World.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.640
While she didn't reveal the scene in which
the accident happened, Alexander did tell

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:29.920
MTV that she majorly damaged her back in the
accident: "I herniated a disk in my Thoracic

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:35.900
spine, dislocated my left shoulder, tore my
right Rhomboid, and chipped eleven vertebra….The

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:41.240
next morning I got in a car to go to the hospital,
and I sat in the car and compressed my spine

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:44.969
a little bit, and went paralyzed in my right
leg and my right hand.

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:46.980
So I was in the hospital for a week."

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.420
Kate Winslet

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.200
Considering her character Rose is one of the
few people who survives the sinking of the

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.840
Titanic, it would have been grimly ironic
if Kate Winslet hadn't even survived filming

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.160
the 1997 blockbuster classic.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.880
But during the scene where Winslet and Leonardo
DiCaprio flee the flooded lower decks, Winslet

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:10.019
was dragged underwater and was unable to come
up for air after her coat got caught on a

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:10.840
metal gate.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.340
Winslet was traumatized by the near death
experience, but director James Cameron?

00:02:15.349 --> 00:02:20.150
He let her catch her breath and then set up
for another take, since Winslet had just ruined

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.600
that one with her silly near-death experience.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:24.360
Jim Caviezel

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:30.829
Mel Gibson's 2004 epic The Passion of the
Christ electrified audiences, energizing the

00:02:30.829 --> 00:02:35.900
faithful and turning the film into one of
the most unlikely hit films in Hollywood history.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.960
But things were even more electrified on set,
as the man who played Jesus himself, Jim Caviezel,

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.980
was struck by an honest-to-God lightning bolt
while filming the sermon on the mount.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.180
He told the 700 Club "I was lit up like a
Christmas tree!

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.480
… What [the extras] saw was fire coming
out the right and left side of my head.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.200
Illumination around the whole body."

00:02:56.569 --> 00:02:57.700
Was it the wrath of God?

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.400
Or was Caviezel simply standing on a hill
during a lightning storm?

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.500
Who can say?

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.160
Martin Sheen

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.760
They say war is hell, but war never visited
the set of Apocalypse Now.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:13.840
The infamously troubled production drove plenty
of people—including director Francis Ford

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.819
Coppola and star Marlon Brando—to the brink
of insanity.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:18.560
"did they tell you?"

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:28.080
"They told me, that you had gone totally insane."

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:33.620
But the one event that came the closest to
grinding the production to a standstill was

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:36.870
36-year-old Martin Sheen's heart attack in
the middle of the jungle.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:41.360
According to the Daily Mail, the crew found
the film's lead actor "crawling along a road

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.160
looking for help."

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:47.099
As Coppola relates it, that incident was nearly
the final straw that sent him into a nervous

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:47.780
breakdown.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.020
He told Rolling Stone:

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.950
"Marty's heart attack… severely traumatized
my nervous system.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:54.879
We didn't know if he was going to make it."

00:03:54.879 --> 00:03:59.920
If Coppola thinks his nervous system was traumatized,
imagine how Sheen must have felt after, you

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.840
know, actually suffering the heart attack!

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.189
Thanks for watching!

